+# Research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15. The deterministic artifact follows the pinned snapshot where a live page may later differ.
+
+| Broadcom page | URL | Architecture decision informed |
+|---|---|---|
+| Upgrade Option for Aria Operations 8.18.4 to VCF Operations 9.0 is greyed out in Aria Suite Lifecycle Manager | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/408461 | Aria Operations 8.18.4 must not land on 9.0.0; select VCF Operations 9.0.1 or later directly. |
+| After upgrading Aria Operations from 8.18.3 to 8.18.4, duplicate objects for vSphere adapter are found. | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/407152/after-upgrading-aria-operations-from-818.html | Remove the incompatible, end-of-support SDDC Health management pack before the VCF Operations transition and preserve native monitoring instead. |
+| Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314 | Use a fresh parallel Logs deployment, recreate integrations, and transfer no more than 90 days of log data. |
+| Upgrade VMware Aria Suite Lifecycle 8.18 to VCF Fleet Manager 9.0 | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433436/upgrade-vmware-aria-suite-lifecycle-818.html | Patch Aria Suite Lifecycle to 8.18 Patch 2 before the VCF 9 management-component transition. |
+| When upgrading Aria Automation 8.18.1 to VCFA 9.0, precheck fails with message - Unsupported cloud accounts of type NSX-V, NSX-T manager mode, or VCF with embedded NSX-T manager mode are present in the VCF Automation host | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/396627 | Preserve NSX Policy-mode integration but remove the unsupported NSX Manager-mode cloud account and its dependent template before upgrade. |
+| VCF Operations 9.0 Sizing Guidelines | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/397782 | Select medium Operations analytics and a three-node medium Logs cluster; keep HA nodes on separate hosts and size Logs from per-node ingestion and connection limits. |
+| Customer sees CPU and Memory allocated to the VM components are too large to run on one NUMA node. It results in high CPU "READY". Customer wants to reduce the CPU and Memory allocated to VM Component. want help in resizing those. | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/412468/customer-sees-cpu-and-memory-allocated-t.html | Retain the supported VCF Automation appliance sizing from the system requirements instead of manually reducing its resources, and separate clustered nodes across hosts. |
+| End of General Support for VMware Aria Operations 8.18 | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422643/end-of-general-support-for-vmware-aria-o.html | Apply the published 2027-10-11 EOGS boundary to the inventoried Aria Operations 8.18.4 release. |
+| Build numbers and versions for VMware Aria Automation (formerly vRealize Automation) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/318130/build-numbers-and-versions-for-vmware-ar.html | Apply the exact Aria Automation 8.18.1 EOGS date of 2027-10-11. |
+| Product Lifecycle matrix for Aria Suite | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/381187/product-lifecycle-matrix-for-aria-suite.html | Check the Operations for Logs 8.18.3 lifecycle entry and apply its 2027-10-11 EOGS boundary. |
+
+The reachable live publications agreed with the pinned authority on the decisions recorded above; no live-source difference changed the deterministic plan.
